{
  "analysis": "Starting fresh in the terminal. I need to examine the input files to understand the source video, segments, transcripts, target language, and reference text. Then I'll need to generate dubbed audio with proper LUFS normalization, create the final video, and generate a report.",
  "plan": "First, I'll examine all input files to understand: 1) The video properties, 2) The segment timings from segments.srt, 3) The source text, 4) The target language, and 5) The reference target text. Then I'll plan the dubbing workflow.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /root/\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /root/target_language.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /root/segments.srt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /root/source_text.srt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /root/reference_target_text.srt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the input files clearly now. Target language is 'ja' (Japanese). There's one segment from 0 to 12.116 seconds. The source text is English and the reference target text is in Japanese. I need to check the video properties and then set up the dubbing workflow.",
  "plan": "1) Check video properties with ffprobe to get duration and audio specs, 2) Create output directories, 3) Generate TTS audio for the Japanese text, 4) Normalize audio to ITU-R BS.1770-4 standard (LUFS), 5) Replace audio in video, 6) Generate the report.json. I'll use available TTS tools and ffmpeg for audio/video processing.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ffprobe -v quiet -print_format json -show_format -show_streams /root/input.mp4\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p /outputs/tts_segments\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which espeak-ng\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which gtts-cli\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which piper\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import pyttsx3; print('pyttsx3 available')\"\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "Video is 12.052 seconds with stereo 16kHz audio. I have espeak-ng available. I need to generate Japanese TTS audio. Let me check for other TTS options and Python packages available.",
  "plan": "Check for available Python TTS libraries (gTTS, edge-tts, etc.) and install if needed. Then generate the Japanese audio, ensure it's 12.116 seconds (matching the segment duration), normalize to LUFS standard, convert to 48kHz mono, and create the final video.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import gtts; print('gtts available')\"\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "pip3 list | grep -i tts\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "pip3 list | grep -i audio\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which ffmpeg\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

